/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::enableAnimationPose(string referenceAnimation)
\brief Enable pose access using a reference clip.

Builds a stable rig from the selected Spriter entity and reference clip. The rig requires compatible bone, image, point, and box tracks with a fixed hierarchy. Nested entities and changing hierarchies are unsupported. On success, clears previous bone overrides, modifiers, IK controllers, custom drawings, and debug flags. A failed attempt preserves the previous enabled pose and records a diagnostic.

\param referenceAnimation Name of an existing reference clip in the current Spriter entity.

\return True on success; false if the rig cannot be enabled. Read getAnimationRigError() after failure.

\note Load Spriter data and select its entity first. Call outside animation callbacks and disable animation physics before replacing the rig.

\par Example
\code{.js}
if (!sprite.enableAnimationPose('reference')) {
    throw new Error(sprite.getAnimationRigError());
}
const boneNames = sprite.getAnimationBoneNames();
\endcode

\see disableAnimationPose(), getAnimationPose(), getAnimationRigError()
*/
